[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
OpenProject %%VERSION%% is installed at %%WWWDIR%%.

This is a native CloudBSD Rails port. Puma binds 127.0.0.1:3000.
nginx terminates TLS and must send X-Forwarded-Proto https.
OPENPROJECT_HOST__NAME defaults to track.cloudbsd.org.

1. Copy JSON config:

     cp %%PREFIX%%/etc/cloudbsd/openproject/config.json.sample \
        %%PREFIX%%/etc/cloudbsd/openproject/config.json

2. Secrets (mode 0600; do not commit):

     openssl rand -hex 64 \
       > %%PREFIX%%/etc/cloudbsd/openproject/secret_key_base
     chmod 0600 %%PREFIX%%/etc/cloudbsd/openproject/secret_key_base
     # write the PostgreSQL password to postgres.password, mode 0600

3. PostgreSQL 16 or 17 (matching the port option):

     createuser -P openproject
     createdb -O openproject openproject

4. Enable memcached and nginx. Merge
   %%PREFIX%%/etc/nginx/openproject.conf.sample
   into the jail vhost (certbot already on track).

5. First-time schema:

     openproject env
     openproject migrate

6. Check and start:

     openproject doctor
     sysrc openproject_enable=YES
     service openproject start

Man pages: openproject(8), openproject.conf(5)
JSON:      %%PREFIX%%/etc/cloudbsd/openproject/config.json
EOM
}
]
